/*! @brief A plain-object dictionary of string values, keyed by name

 StringMap is the typed form of the string dictionaries exposed and accepted by
 the runtime: `http.STATUS_CODES`, `HttpClient#proxyEnv`, the `proxyEnv`
 argument of `http.setGlobalProxyFromEnv` and the return value of
 `util.parseEnv`. It is a regular JavaScript object dictionary (not an ES
 `Map`); the property names are environment variable, status-code or option
 names. `process.env` stays a plain object because it is a live view of the
 operating system environment, not a snapshot dictionary.

 The runtime reads a missing key as `undefined`, while the TypeScript index
 signature is `string`; use `hasOwnProperty` or a truthiness check when a
 missing entry must be distinguished from the empty string.

 Example 1 — parse an environment file:
 ```JavaScript
 const util = require('util');

 const env = util.parseEnv('A=1\nB="two words"');
 console.log(env.A, env.B); // 1 two words
 ```

 Example 2 — read the process environment:
 ```JavaScript
 console.log(typeof process.env.PATH); // string
 ```
*/
map StringMap: String;
